        "node_id": "n_15_7cf874",
        "thought_text": "Use a breadth-first search (BFS) or depth-first search (DFS) to explore all possible sequences of adjacent swaps, keeping track of visited states to avoid redundant calculations. This ensures finding the minimum number of swaps efficiently.",
